{{/*
  import — one import's progress, as the one row it is.

  A hundred-megabyte bundle takes long enough that silence reads as failure,
  so the answer is a stream rather than one answer at the end: the handler
  renders this region again, and flushes it, for every state a run reaches
  (internal/app/importing.go). Each render replaces the last -- the `import`
  partial target is an outerMorph over this section -- so what the reader sees
  is one row changing its mind, not a growing list, and the section itself is
  the same element throughout, which is what lets `aria-live` announce the
  changes to a reader who is not watching the corner.

  The row's id carries the run's number: within a run the morph finds the same
  element and updates it, and a second run brings a different element, which
  is how its dismissal starts over instead of inheriting one that has already
  played out.

  With no rows the section renders itself away. That is a first paint, where
  no import has happened yet -- and it is also how a cancelled picker leaves:
  the handler's last word is this region with nothing in it.
*/}}
{{define "import"}}<section id="atlas-import" class="import-rows" aria-live="polite"{{if not .Rows}} hidden{{end}}>{{range .Rows}}<p id="atlas-import-run-{{.Run}}" class="import-row{{if .Fading}} import-row-fading{{end}}" data-state="{{.State}}">{{.Detail}}</p>{{end}}</section>
{{end}}
